Problem:
Rotate Image (https://leetcode.com/problems/rotate-image/description/)

Approach:
Extra Matrix (Column-to-Row Transformation)

Why this works:
A 90° clockwise rotation can be achieved by taking each column
of the original matrix from bottom to top and placing it as a row
in the output matrix.

For each column:
- Traverse from the bottom row to the top row.
- Store the elements in the corresponding row of the output matrix.

After constructing the rotated matrix, we use matrix[:] = output
to replace the contents of the original matrix while keeping the
same matrix object.

Time Complexity:
O(n²)
Every element of the matrix is visited exactly once.

Space Complexity:
O(n²)
An additional n × n matrix is created to store the rotated matrix.

# ----------------------------------
# Extra Matrix (Column-to-Row Transformation)
# ----------------------------------

class Solution:
    def rotate(self, matrix: List[List[int]]) -> None:
        output = [[0] * len(matrix) for _ in range(len(matrix))]

        row = 0
        for i in range(len(matrix)):
            col = 0
            for j in range(len(matrix) - 1, -1, -1):
                output[row][col] = matrix[j][i]
                col += 1
            row += 1

        matrix[:] = output
